-- title:
--   Compatible sections of the unramified quotient are determined by chart values
-- statement:
--   The statement is an injectivity assertion about sections over the chart opens of a tower-quotient of the unramified presentation of a Mumford tower. Its data and hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Base arithmetic.** A prime $r$; a commutative domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an element $\pi$ of $\mathcal O$ with `hπ` asserting $\pi$ irreducible, `hcomplete` asserting that $\mathcal O$ is adically complete for the ideal $(\pi)$, `hres` asserting $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi)) = r$ and `hunr` asserting $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$; a field $K_0$ of characteristic zero which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified extension with Frobenius.** A commutative domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of characteristic zero which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to: `hOnr_complete` ($O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$), `hOnr_max` (that ideal is maximal), `hOnr_alg` (every $x \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $(\pi)$), `hOnr_closed` (every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $(\pi)$) and `hFr` ($\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo $(\pi)$ for all $x$).
--
--   **Valuation of the determinant.** A group homomorphism $v_{\det} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) with `hvdet`: $v_{\det}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Group-theoretic data.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and a subgroup $\Gamma \le G$, with `hcent` (some $z \in \Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix $c \cdot 1$ and $v_{\det}(\sigma z) = 2$) and `hodd` (some $w \in \Gamma$ has $v_{\det}(\sigma w) = 1$); a subgroup $\Gamma'$ characterised by `hΓ'` as the set of $x \in \Gamma$ with $v_{\det}(\sigma x)$ even. A homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ with `hρ` identifying $\rho g$ with the class of $\sigma g$, and, for the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ acting on the vertices of the lattice tree of $(\mathcal O, K_0)$, `hdisc` (all vertex stabilisers are finite) and `hcocpt` (a finite set of vertices meets every orbit). An element $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with `hg₁`: its matrix is $\mathrm{diag}(\pi, 1)$. A subgroup $N$ of $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ with `hNle` ($N \le \rho(\Gamma')$), `hNnorm` ($N$ is normal in $\rho(\Gamma)$) and `hNidx` (the relative index of $N$ in $\rho(\Gamma')$ is non-zero). A term `DM : MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`, i.e. a tower of schemes $Z_n$ with proper flat structure maps $\mathrm{zb}_n$ to $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$, cartesian transition maps $\mathrm{zt}_n$, affine neighbourhoods of finite sets, and a family of $B$-points $\mathrm{q}_n$ indexed by Deligne data over $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ killed by $\pi^{n+1}$ — a Deligne datum being a choice, for every full lattice $M$ in $K_0^2$, of a $B$-submodule of the base-changed lattice with invertible quotient, monotone in $M$, equivariant for homotheties and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$ — natural in $B$, compatible with the transition maps, invariant under pullback of Deligne data by elements of $N$, together with the charting axioms of that structure.
--
--   **The tower $X$ with its two projections.** Schemes $X_n$ with maps $\mathrm{xb}_n : X_n \to \mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and $\mathrm{xt}_n : X_n \to X_{n+1}$; a finite group $G_2$ acting through $a_n : G_2 \to \mathrm{Aut}(X_n)$; projections $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n} : X_n \to Z_n$ and $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n} : X_n \to \mathrm{Spec}$ of $E/(\pi)^{n+1}$, where $E$ is the equaliser subalgebra of $\mathrm{Fr}\circ\mathrm{Fr}$ and the identity on $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (the $\mathrm{Fr}^2$-fixed subring); a homomorphism $\theta : \Gamma \to G_2$ and $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphisms $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ of $E/(\pi)^{n+1}$. The hypotheses are: `hcart` (each square $\mathrm{xt}_n$, $\mathrm{xb}_n$, $\mathrm{xb}_{n+1}$ over the quotient map $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+2} \to \mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ is a pullback), `hproper` and `hflat` (each $\mathrm{xb}_n$ is proper, resp. flat), `haff` (every finite subset of $X_n$ lies in an affine open), `ha_over` and `ha_xt` (the $G_2$-action is over the base and commutes with the transition maps), `hX` (each $X_n$ is the pullback of $\mathrm{zb}_n$ along $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the reduction $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1} \to E/(\pi)^{n+1}$, via $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}, \mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$), `hxb` ($\mathrm{xb}_n = \mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ followed by $\mathrm{zb}_n$), `hxt₁` and `hxt₂` (compatibility of the two projections with the transition maps), `hθsurj` ($\theta$ is surjective), `hθker` ($\theta\gamma = 1$ iff $\rho\gamma \in N$), `hFr₂` ($\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ is induced by $\mathrm{Fr}$ on $E$), `ha_pr₂` (the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$ equals $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$ followed by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}^{-v_{\det}(\sigma\gamma)}$), and `ha_pr₁` (for $\gamma \in \Gamma$, $B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi^{n+1} = 0$ and Deligne data $P, P'$ over $B$ with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ by $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, any $x : \mathrm{Spec}\,B \to X_n$ with $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ equal to $\mathrm{q}_n(P)$ satisfies that $x$ followed by $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ and then $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ equals $\mathrm{q}_n(P')$).
--
--   **The quotient datum downstairs.** A term `DQ : TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a`: schemes $Y_n$ with proper flat maps $\mathrm{yb}_n$ to $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and cartesian transitions $\mathrm{yt}_n$, together with finite surjective $G_2$-invariant maps $\mathrm{p}_n : X_n \to Y_n$ over the base, cartesian against the transitions, epimorphic after restriction to any open, and satisfying the local universal property and the remaining axioms of that structure. Moreover a family $\mathrm q$ assigning, to each $n$, each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1} = 0$ and each pair consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$, a $B$-point of $Y_n$, subject to: `hqdef` (if $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and $\psi_2 : E/(\pi)^{n+1} \to B$ agree in the sense of `hψ₂`, and $x : \mathrm{Spec}\,B \to X_n$ satisfies $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{1,n}$ equals $\mathrm q_n(P)$ and $x$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{2,n}$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}(\psi_2)$, then $\mathrm q_n(\psi, P) = x$ followed by $\mathrm p_n$), `hqover` (the points lie over $\mathrm{Spec}\,B \to \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$), `hqnat` (naturality in $B$), `hqyt` (compatibility with the transition maps $\mathrm{yt}_n$) and `hqinv` (invariance: if $\gamma \in \Gamma$ and $x, x'$ satisfy `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct`, i.e. the first components differ by the Frobenius twist by $-v_{\det}(\sigma\gamma)$ and the second component of $x'$ is the pullback of that of $x$ by $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, then $\mathrm q_n(x') = \mathrm q_n(x)$).
--
--   **The unramified layer.** A term `Pr : MumfordTower.NrPresentation … ((Γ'.subgroupOf Γ).map θ)`, providing a tower $X'_n$ over $\mathrm{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)^{n+1})$ with transitions $\mathrm{xt}'_n$, a $G_2$-action $a'_n$, comparison maps $\mathrm{qX}_n : X'_n \to X_n$ making the base squares cartesian and compatible with transitions and the action, and charts $\kappa'_{h,n}$ from $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $A_n := \bigl(\mathrm{chartERing}\,O^{\mathrm{nr}}\,\pi\,r\bigr)/(\pi)^{n+1}$ to $X'_n$, indexed by $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, satisfying the axioms of that structure. A term `D' : TowerQuotientDatum Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) Pr.X' Pr.xb' Pr.xt' G₂ Pr.a'`, with schemes $Y'_n$, transitions $\mathrm{yt}'_n$ and quotient maps $\mathrm p'_n : X'_n \to Y'_n$ as above. Comparison morphisms $\mathrm{rY}_n : Y'_n \to Y_n$ with `hrY` (the squares against the base maps and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the reduction $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1} \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)^{n+1}$ are pullbacks), `hrY_p` ($\mathrm p'_n$ followed by $\mathrm{rY}_n$ equals $\mathrm{qX}_n$ followed by $\mathrm p_n$) and `hrY_yt` (compatibility with the transitions).
--
--   **Chart opens and chart restriction.** For every $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and $n$, an open $U_{h,n}$ of $Y'_n$ with `hU`: its underlying set is the image of the base map of $\kappa'_{h,n}$ followed by $\mathrm p'_n$; a ring homomorphism $c_{h,n}$ from the sections of $Y'_n$ over $U_{h,n}$ to $A_n$; `hκU`: the preimage of $U_{h,n}$ under $\kappa'_{h,n}$ followed by $\mathrm p'_n$ is all of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_n$; and `hc`: for any witness of $\top \le$ that preimage, $c_{h,n}$ is the pullback of sections along $\kappa'_{h,n}$ followed by $\mathrm p'_n$, restricted to $\top$ and transported along the canonical isomorphism between global sections of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_n$ and $A_n$. Finally an element $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is fixed.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For all families $s, s'$ assigning to each $m \in \mathbb N$ a section of the structure sheaf of $Y'_m$ over $U_{h,m}$, if
--
--   (i) for every $m$ and every witness $\mathrm{hle}$ of $U_{h,m} \le (\mathrm{yt}'_m)^{-1}(U_{h,m+1})$, the restriction along $\mathrm{hle}$ of the image of $s(m+1)$ under the sheaf map of $\mathrm{yt}'_m$ on $U_{h,m+1}$ equals $s(m)$;
--
--   (ii) the same condition holds for $s'$; and
--
--   (iii) $c_{h,m}(s(m)) = c_{h,m}(s'(m))$ for every $m$;
--
--   then $s = s'$ as functions of $m$.
--
--   This is the injectivity half of the "functions" clause in the construction of the unramified layer of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: a compatible family of sections over the chart opens of the quotient tower $Y'$ is determined by its chart values in the rings $A_m$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions), and the proof proceeds from the description of the fibres of $\mathrm p'_m$ as $G_2$-orbits given by [`AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.p_base_eq_iff_and_preimage_image_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.p_base_eq_iff_and_preimage_image_eq).
